  "synonym_discrimination": null,
  "usage_note": "The number of a **century** is one more than the first figures of its years: in everyday use, the years 1900 to 1999 are *the twentieth century*. Strictly, a century begins in a year ending in *01*, so the twentieth century ran from 1901 to 2000. *The 1900s* means the years 1900 to 1999.",
